# Hand-edited copy of omnikey-profiles.log: a healthy card never sends
# profileInfoListError for an unrestricted ProfileInfoListRequest (an
# empty search asks for "every profile," which a well-behaved ISD-R can
# always answer, empty or not), so this failure cannot be captured from
# real hardware -- exactly the case testdata/cards/README.md's own
# "What is safe to commit" section describes recordings existing for.
#
# The only change from omnikey-profiles.log: the STORE DATA response for
# BF2D00 now carries ProfileInfoListError (tag '81', IMPLICIT INTEGER,
# incorrectInputValues == 1: '81 01 01') instead of profileInfoListOk
# ('A0 00', an empty SEQUENCE OF). The SELECT ISD-R exchange above it is
# untouched, real-hardware bytes, so this recording still exercises the
# real ISD-R selection path and only fakes the one answer this project
# cannot otherwise get a card to give.
